{"id":29450,"slug":"wanda","title":"Wanda","year":1970,"country":"United States","duration":103,"spine":965,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29450-wanda","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/6b94d52257de3f4b10d82fc0ff759d18/NtDa9MzcQMLF4K8R6XPI7DuDWWnNhM_large.jpg","description":"\nWith her first and only feature film—a hard-luck drama she wrote, directed, and starred in—Barbara Loden turned in a groundbreaking work of American independent cinema, bringing to life a kind of character seldom seen on-screen. Set amid a soot-choked Pennsylvania landscape, and shot in an intensely intimate vérité style, the film takes up with distant and soft-spoken Wanda (Loden), who has left her husband, lost custody of her children, and now finds herself alone, drifting between dingy bars and motels, where she falls prey to a series of callous men—including a bank robber who ropes her into his next criminal scheme. An until now difficult-to-see masterpiece that has nonetheless exerted an outsize influence on generations of artists and filmmakers, Wanda is a compassionate and wrenching portrait of a woman stranded on society’s margins.\nWanda was restored by the UCLA Film & Television Archive. Restoration funding provided by Gucci and The Film Foundation.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Barbara Loden","slug":"barbara-loden"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Barbara Loden","role":"Wanda","slug":"barbara-loden"},{"actor":"Michael Higgins","role":"Mr. Dennis","slug":"michael-higgins"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Barbara Loden","slug":"barbara-loden"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Barbara Loden","slug":"barbara-loden"},{"role":"Photographed by","person":"Proferes Nicholas T.","slug":null},{"role":"Edited by","person":"Proferes Nicholas T.","slug":null},{"role":"Lighting and sound","person":"Lars Hedman","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant","person":"Christopher Cronyn","slug":null},{"role":"Sound editor","person":"Harvey Greenstein","slug":null},{"r